url: 'https://github.com/GuiloScion/NexusOS'
abstract: >-
  NexusOS is an x86-64 operating system written from scratch with
  no external bootloader, kernel framework, or tutorial
  scaffolding. It comprises a custom 512-byte MBR bootloader
  carrying the machine from real mode through protected mode to
  long mode, a full interrupt descriptor table, a physical frame
  allocator and four-level paging virtual memory manager, a
  demand-grown heap, a preemptive round-robin scheduler with
  mutexes, counting semaphores and condition variables, an
  interrupt-driven PIO ATA driver, a read-only FAT12 filesystem,
  and a compositing window manager. Build Your Own Operating
  System is the companion course in docs/book, which walks a
  reader through constructing the system stage by stage.
keywords:
